An account gains its units every tick without a limit.
A thread idle for long would come back with a burst that keeps every other thread waiting;
no account holds more than its cap.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a place's account holds more than its cap
Witness: fuzz lend-lender-unbound

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -204,8 +204,7 @@ static uint32_t account_now(const struct place *p)
         return account_cap(p);
     }
     uint64_t balance = p->balance + (uint64_t)passed * tick_gain(p);
-    uint32_t cap = account_cap(p);
-    return balance > cap ? cap : (uint32_t)balance;
+    return (uint32_t)balance;
 }
 
 /* Bring a place's account up to the count; inline, since every switch calls it and clang stopped inlining it alone. */
